  "summary": "Appliqué parade flags of Fante asafo companies — proverbs, warriors and lions stitched in loud color.",
  "description": "Asafo are the traditional military companies of Fante towns, and their frankaa flags turn that rivalry into appliqué spectacle: cotton figures cut and stitched on loud grounds — British lions disemboweled, warriors rowing past Europeans, proverbs rendered as literal pictures. Companies commissioned flags from specialist artists for festivals and funerals, keeping scores against rival companies. European trade cloth and heraldry meet Akan proverb wit on every banner.",
